      "info": {
        "auth": false,
        "description": "The keyless GET side of Kavel's anonymous AI image API: polling a generation task for its status and result image URLs. Anonymous output is 1K and watermarked.\n\nSources: https://kavel.readthedocs.io/en/latest/sdk/http/ and the reference it links, https://hanshs474.gitbook.io/kavel-api/kavel-anonymous-image-api.md, with the poll endpoint probed live on 2026-10-23 using the task id from that reference (2a04f52a-0da3-4629-8a3f-ecc5a507f34f), which still answers with a finished result, and with an unknown task id.\n\nNOT modelled: POST /api/ai/generate, which submits a job and is the only way to obtain a new task id. It is not GET, it spends credits from a small per-client wallet (15 credits; 5 per text-to-image, 15 per edit) under a 30-credit per-IP daily ceiling, and it was not probed. Without it this spec can only read tasks whose id is already known. Observed but unexplained: the image URL in a finished task changed between two polls of the same task. The `x-anon-id` header the docs say to send on the poll is not required: the probe without it returned the same result. Unverified: the item type of `videos` (always empty; assumed URL strings) and any status other than success.",
        "meta_source": "https://www.freepublicapis.com",
        "servers": [
          {
            "url": "https://www.kavel.ai"
          }
        ],
        "summary": "The keyless GET side of Kavel's anonymous AI image API: polling a generation task for its status and result image URLs.",
        "title": "Kavel Anonymous Task API",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "website": "https://hanshs474.gitbook.io/kavel-api/kavel-anonymous-image-api"
      },
